#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Architecture decision dossier generator (Lane 27): the current status of hall_only / rf_hall / ecr_hall.

It assembles, from repository files only, the architecture-decision dossier and writes

    docs/architecture_comparison/dossier/dossier.json         (machine-readable; schema architecture_decision_dossier_v1)
    docs/architecture_comparison/dossier/DECISION_DOSSIER.md  (a pure rendering of dossier.json)

The dossier is a STATUS, NOT A DECISION. It ranks, scores and selects nothing. An architecture is reported as eliminated
only when the hard-gate evaluator (abep_sim/hard_gates.py, via its committed status file) eliminates it on a binding gate,
and the dossier re-checks that claim against the per-gate verdicts. A selection is presented only if the gate logic
eliminates all but one architecture AND the owner has recorded a decision for that one
(docs/architecture_comparison/dossier/owner_decision_record.json). Neither holds today.

Rules the generator enforces (CLAUDE.md rules 3, 6, 10; docs/EVIDENCE.md):
- Every expected input is looked up at its repository-relative path. A missing input is listed as UNRESOLVED with what it
  would provide; nothing is filled in for it. There are no default physical or efficiency values in this file.
- A malformed input of a known contract (wrong schema id, inconsistent elimination claim, malformed owner record) raises;
  it is never skipped silently.
- Every file read is hashed (sha256 of its bytes) in the provenance section, with the generation time and git commit.
- The output is deterministic apart from provenance.generated_at (and the git state recorded next to it).
- Screening candidates (sgb-screen-*) and unadmitted Hall closures are never performance sources: quantity records that
  mention a screening candidate are excluded from the quantity census and counted as excluded.

Preview mode (--preview-overlay DIR, repeatable) resolves inputs that are missing from --root in other checkouts (for
example unmerged lane worktrees), READ-ONLY. A preview must be written outside the repository (--out-dir); it can never
overwrite the committed dossier. The hard-gate evaluator is re-run (python -B -m abep_sim.hard_gates status, without
writing bytecode) in the checkout it was resolved from, to confirm that the committed status file is current.

Usage:
    python scripts/architecture/build_decision_dossier.py                  # regenerate the committed dossier
    python scripts/architecture/build_decision_dossier.py --check          # exit 1 if the committed dossier is stale
    python scripts/architecture/build_decision_dossier.py --out-dir /tmp/x --preview-overlay ../other-worktree
"""
